  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\von.neumann.omega]\nDefines: omega is \\set\nexpresses:\n. let:\n  . (.A is \\(inductive)::set.)[:1:]\n  . X is \\set\n  then:\n  . have: X \"in\"? omega\n    iff:\n    . X \"in\"? A\n    . forAll: I is \\(inductive)::set\n      then: X \"in\"? I\nEnables:\n. capability: X_ \"in\" omega :-> X_ is \\set\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Von Neumann Numerals\"\n. written: \"\\omega\"\n. description: \"The set $\\omega$ of all Von Neumann numerals, the smallest\n                inductive set.\"\nJustification:\n. [1]\n  have: A is \\(inductive)::set\n  by: \\axiom.of.infinity\nId: \"c13f4641-0ed5-4ad7-b309-8ec13b4c6b77\"",
